---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/* One booking target, shared with the homepage call CTA. */
const booking =
  'https://calendar.google.com/calendar/appointments/schedules/AcZssZ0V1VeplVknT4zFIM0By-Xi-ryDNX0QpZ_qRR2DWt31DLwnxmQfTErXpuV99tVkZ2FHKOgDEuB-';
---

<Base
  title="Nomoro — Finance and insurance flows"
  description="A quote, a claim, a loan application, an investor onboarding. In two weeks I give you the number, where people stop, and what to fix first. Fixed price, one flow."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <section class="pt-24 pb-24 sm:pt-40 sm:pb-32">
      <h1 class="display measure">You have a customer flow shipping and no number on it yet.</h1>
      <p class="lede measure mt-6" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">
        A quote, a claim, a loan application, an investor onboarding, a broker portal. The date is
        in the plan. Someone will ask how many people got through. In two weeks I give you the
        number, where they stop, and what to fix first.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-9">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={booking} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Book a 30-minute call</a
        >
      </p>
      <p class="micro measure mt-8">
        Three years on new user activation at Hootsuite. Finance and insurance flows since my EY
        years. One flow at a time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ The situation ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">The situation</p>
      <h2 class="headline measure mt-3">Does this sound like you?</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <p>
          You're rebuilding a flow brokers or customers have to get through. Car. Home. A loan
          application. An investor onboarding. Go-live is set. The squad is full. The CX programme
          expects an adoption number this year and nobody can say what it is today, let alone after
          launch.
        </p>
        <p>
          You've looked at the options. The agency sends three people for three months and a deck.
          The analytics vendor sees its own tool. Ship and see means the first number you get is a
          complaint from a broker.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ What you get ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">What you get</p>
      <h2 class="headline measure mt-3">Two weeks. One flow. Three things.</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">The number.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Time to first quote, first application, first deposit. Measured on your data, in your
            tools. If it isn't measured today, measuring it is the first deliverable.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">The leak.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Where brokers or customers stop, step by step, and what each stop costs. From your
            analytics, your session data where you have it, and five real people going through the
            flow while I watch.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">The first fix.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            A ranked backlog. The top item specified to the level your squad can build next sprint.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="measure mt-8">
        What you don't get: bodies, a three-month proposal, a dashboard you need me to read. I work
        in your tools. Nothing new gets installed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ How it runs ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">How it runs</p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <p>
          Week one: define the number with the team lead, read what the data already says, sit with
          brokers or customers going through the flow. Week two: leak map, cost per stop, backlog,
          readout to whoever owns the number. Two fixed days a week, on site where it helps.
        </p>
        <p>
          Fixed price, scoped in writing to one flow. Get in touch for an offer. Paid on signature,
          fourteen days. Anything outside scope is quoted before it starts. If the readout says your
          squad can fix it alone, that is the right outcome.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Proof ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">Proof</p>
      <h2 class="headline measure mt-3">Two flows, same method.</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Capitac, investment platform, Belgium.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Investor onboarding and application on a two-sided platform in a regulated environment:
            the path from first visit to a completed, compliant application. Design and shipped UX
            beside product and engineering, 2026.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3 class="headline text-[1.125rem]">Insurer's broker platform, Non-life.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
            Two broker sales flows, Car and Home. Activation Diagnostic started October 2026: the
            number, the leak, the first fix. Named here when the client agrees.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="measure mt-8">
        Before Nomoro: insurance and banking flows at EY Studio+ and EY VODW for Belfius, Corona
        Direct and Baloise. Three years at Hootsuite owning design for net-new user activation.
      </p>
      <div class="card mt-8 max-w-2xl">
        <p class="font-[610]">On numbers.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
          I don't publish lifts I can't source.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Not for you if ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-32">
      <p class="kicker">Not for you if</p>
      <ul class="rows measure mt-6 text-[0.9375rem] leading-normal">
        <li>There's no flow with a date</li>
        <li>Nobody will own the number</li>
        <li>You want a BA for twelve months</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="measure mt-6" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">
        That last one is a real conversation, and I'll say so on the call.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ Close ============ -->
    <section class="pb-24 sm:pb-28">
      <h2 class="headline measure">
        Is what you have good enough to put a number on it by the date?
      </h2>
      <p class="lede measure mt-6" style="color: var(--ink-soft)">
        If yes, you don't need me. If not, thirty minutes.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={booking} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book the call</a>
        <a class="micro underline underline-offset-2" href="mailto:jelle@nomoro.be"
          >jelle@nomoro.be</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
